# Browser
# Tranquil Frillback at a table, Bot1 a browser page: "you may pay {G} up to three times" is one payment whose number of times
# the dock's stepper sets (CR 603.12a) - it says it goes up to three, and its pay button names the cost at the number shown.
# The page is read as the line that pays is played, its + already clicked to twice: {G}{G} is paid. The reflexive ability's
# dock then asks to "choose up to two" (CR 700.2b), and Bot1 destroys Bot2's Sol Ring and gains 4 life.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Tranquil Frillback
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Sol Ring
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tranquil Frillback.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Tranquil Frillback: pay {G} up to three times?
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = When you do, choose up to that many: destroy target artifact or enchantment, exile target player's graveyard, you gain 4 life  ·  2 times, so {G}{G}  ·  − and + change how many times (up to three)  ·  {G}{G} is covered
? Client.Bot1.Button.Pay {G}{G}.Enabled = true
Bot1.PayCost(Times: 2)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Tranquil Frillback: choose up to two
Bot1.Modes(1; 3)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
Bot1.Pass

